"""make_claims.py — writes CLAIMS.md from generated/ledger_rows.json (the ledger rows the page prints, evaluated by build.mjs) and claims_anchors.json.
The claim text is therefore the page's text (ja), never copied by hand; each K row lists the anchors that look at its place. Run after `bun build.mjs`.
    python3 -I make_claims.py
"""
import json
import pathlib

HERE = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
led = json.loads((HERE / "generated" / "ledger_rows.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
anchors = json.loads((HERE / "claims_anchors.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
ja, en = led["ja"]["rows"], led["en"]["rows"]
assert [r["id"] for r in ja] == [r["id"] for r in en], "ja and en ledgers carry the same rows"
by = {}
for a in anchors:
    by.setdefault(a["id"][:3], []).append(a)
kinds = {"repo_json_equals": "json", "file_md5": "md5", "derived": "recount", "pack_equals_derived": "pack = recount", "repo_text_contains": "text", "derived_close": "recount (tol)", "pack_close_derived": "pack = recount (tol)", "pack_equals": "pack = card", "here_json_equals": "config", "repo_json_close": "json (tol)", "pack_equals_json": "pack = json"}


def anc(k):
    return ", ".join(f"{a['id']}({kinds[a['kind']]})" for a in by.get(k, []))


L = ["# CLAIMS — what the figure says, where each number comes from (moy-1)", "",
     "Generated by `make_claims.py` from `generated/ledger_rows.json` (the very rows the page prints in its ledger; ja shown) and `claims_anchors.json`. Do not edit by hand.",
     "`check_claims.py` looks at each place: an anchor id (K03a ...) must have a claim row here, and a claim row (K01 ...) must have an anchor.",
     "Levels: **L1** = a copy of a value in a card's output / a frozen verdict · **L2** = a number counted from the card's output (recounted by `check_claims.py` with code written separately from `pack_moy1.py` and `data.mjs`) · **L3** = a reading (whose reading; adoption is the human's) · **×** = not said.",
     "Voice: nothing says what the model \"thought\", \"hesitated over\" or \"noticed\"; a count is where a sentence shape occurs in the text, and a frozen label is the whole text put through the card's classifier.", "",
     "## A. What the figure says (L1 / L2) — with the anchors that look at the place", "", "| id | claim (as the figure prints it, ja) | source (file · key) | anchors |", "|---|---|---|---|"]
for r in ja:
    if r["lv"] == "L1":
        L.append(f"| {r['id']} | {r['text']} | {r['src']} | {anc(r['id'])} |")
L += ["", "## B. Readings (L3) — whose reading; adoption is the human's", "", "| id | reading | source |", "|---|---|---|"]
for r in ja:
    if r["lv"] == "L3":
        L.append(f"| {r['id']} | {r['text']} | {r['src']} |")
L += ["", "## C. What is not said (×) — plain statements, never a small note", "", "| id | not said | source |", "|---|---|---|"]
for r in ja:
    if r["lv"] == "x":
        L.append(f"| {r['id']} | {r['text']} | {r['src']} |")
L += ["", "## D. Corrections between the BRIEF and the data (the data was used)", "",
      "- The BRIEF §0 (chapter 3) says the whole-text label and the answer field differ for \"5 rows\" (the frozen attractors s0, s1, s2, s6, s8). By the answer-field reading the colour also changes on **s4** (frozen stuck-L1; its answer is \"no invariant\"; its text contains the word concyclic only inside a negation). The figure shows 6 rows with a thread and says so (state 5).",
      "- The BRIEF §0 (chapter 3) for open s1 says O1O2 is used \"only in a slope calculation\". The data: the token O1O2 occurs 21 times; 19 of them sit with the words *line* or *slope* within ±80 characters; 1 is the name of the centres in the first lines; 1 is elsewhere; a 'diameter / centre = O1O2' sentence occurs 0 times. The figure says exactly that (K04d), not \"only slope\".",
      "- The inventory's `PRED_O` missed the subscript spelling `O₁O₂`. This entry adds `₁ ₂` to the pattern; the counts the BRIEF gives (open 0 / 10, blocked 7 / 10) do not change.",
      "- Every other value of the BRIEF §6 (V1-V11) agrees with the data (K03e, K05d, K06b, K07d, K11f, K12f, K13c, K14d, K16f, K18c, K20d: the inventory's own recount, read as text).",
      "", "### v2 (BRIEF v2, 2026-10-28 afternoon)", "",
      "- **cmt5's `bind` was written in v1 by the whole-text label only** (thinking path 40 / 40 vs answer path 8 / 40). By the answer-field label (`label_json_fields`) it is **36 / 40 vs 4 / 40** (read.json `labels_full_vs_answer_field`; BRIEF v2 §3; K16g-s, K28). v2 writes both wherever v1 wrote the number (state 8's limits strip, state 22, K16, K28, X01, the criterion of acceptance question 3 in README.md); neither is written alone as \"bind\".",
      "- The card's RESULT olm59 §5-1 says that where He-Hi is named \"no group moves (half and half)\". The table of the same RESULT has the answer-side group at 11 / 34 (−0.043) and the thought-side group at 19 / 34 (K26). R03 therefore restates the reading as \"the median differences are small\"; the RESULT's own sentence is not copied.",
      "- The scene rows are not typical rows: S_O is the shortest generation that satisfies the predicate (thinking path × answer-field bind × both windows inside the generation), S_H likewise (answer-field attractor × He-Hi naming). K23a recounts the selection; X12 says neither is representative nor a matched pair.",
      "- The window: the card's runner is not read here; the convention (before = [e−32, e), after = [e, e+32)) was found by recomputing read.json's Q3 numbers from the arrays (all 24 keys agree: n and counts exactly, medians to 1e-6; K25-K27).", "",
      "", "### v2.1 (BRIEF v2.1, 2026-10-28 evening)", "",
      "- **olm62's rank correlation is computed with ordinal ranks** (argsort of argsort with numpy's default sort), not with tie-averaged ranks. The three values of read.json (O1O2 0.7804792518994741 · He-Hi 0.21161191749427039 · all 162,545 tokens 0.4152617665861453) are reproduced to 1e-12 only by that rule (K32; the card's runner was not opened: the rule was found by trying the usual tie rules). With tie-averaged ranks the same data give 0.781 · 0.221 · 0.489 (`generated/olm62_tie_note.json`, not carried to the pages: it is outside the card). The reading (a clear positive link for O1O2 events, a weak one for He-Hi events) does not change, but the pooled value moves most (0.415 → 0.489) because zeros are very common among the formula-character shares. The figure says only \"the card's rank rule\" (state 22 lim, X15).",
      "- The share of formula characters of a **window** is the mean over its 32 tokens of each token's share (formula characters / characters of the token); this reproduces the counts, the medians and the splits of read.json exactly (K31-K34). The card's C2 reproduces with: digit tokens = ASCII-digit-only tokens (32,498), letter tokens = tokens that are only letters once their spaces are stripped (84,759; a token such as ` the` counts; a plain ASCII-only reading gives 84,683 and does not reproduce the card).",
      "- The tree's zone for the cards outside it is the BRIEF's (before: replication_config_frozen · pc1 · screen bf16 · behavior screen · F5 · moy_suite_report; after: olm59 · olm62). The BRIEF calls the first group \"07-08 month cards\"; the data file `moy_suite_report.json`'s last commit is **06-14** (K42), so the map's box says \"before 10-19\" and shows each card's own date. The date of a card is the date in the name of its record (RESULT / ADJUDICATION), or, for the two data files with no dated record, git's last commit of the file.",
      "- olm62's Q2 threshold (60 %) is read from olm62's own PREREG (K33l), not taken from olm59's Q2 (also 60 %: a different prediction).", "",
      "### v3 (BRIEF v3, 2026-11-06): the four disagreements between the two 10-28 figures, decided from the data", "",
      "- **blocked s8's answer field** (K69 · K06 · K09): the answer field is the last JSON's `conjecture`; s8 has no JSON, so it has none. v2 read its last paragraph as O1O2 (7 / 10 and \"all 10 agree with the frozen label\"); the other figure said \"no JSON\" (O1O2 6 / 10). In cmt5's data the 3 / 3 rows without a `{\"conjecture\"` object all carry `label_json_fields` = B-flail (whole-text labels attractor 2 · bind 1): the frozen rule does not read the last paragraph. So the figure says O1O2 6 · He-Hi 3 · no JSON 1; K06 says 9 of 10 rows agree with the whole-text label.",
      "- **open rows whose colour changes** (K05 · state 5): by the predicate \"the colour of the frozen label differs from the colour of the answer-field reading\": the five frozen attractor rows (s0 s1 s2 s6 s8) and s4 (frozen stuck-L1, answer \"no invariant\") = **6**. The other figure's chip said 5 while its own table marked 6.",
      "- **the date of a card that has only a data file** (K42): git's last commit of the file (moy_suite_report = 06-14), never a month range; the box is \"before 10-19\".",
      "- **the card marks** (K43): v3.1 (entry P's rule, BRIEF v3.1 §2-5): a card is marked on a state iff the state's numbers, verbatim text or drawing are read from that card's frozen output (a number a limit note quotes counts), or the card froze the instrument they are made with (the SAE groups). `build.mjs` derives the marks from the DATA paths each state reads and stops on any difference with `config.json` (`generated/marks_derived.json`); `state_data` -> `card_of_data` says the same and the anchors K43 check every state. A card struck after the 10-28 figure is never a mark on a 10-28 state (the added part shows it in its card table). Against v3: state 8 gains cmt5, 18-20 gain replication_config_frozen, 21 gains olm62.",
      "- The two readers' other disagreements: olm62's Q2 holds two rules in its PREREG (not read below 8 events; threshold 60 %) — both are said (K68); the tie-averaged rank values are shown only as \"a number outside the card\" (K67)."]

(HERE / "CLAIMS.md").write_text("\n".join(L), encoding="utf-8")
print(f"CLAIMS.md written: {sum(1 for r in ja if r['lv']=='L1')} L1 rows · {sum(1 for r in ja if r['lv']=='L3')} L3 · {sum(1 for r in ja if r['lv']=='x')} x · anchors {len(anchors)}")
